{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457681-creating-prosthetics","id":1457681,"title":"Creating Prosthetics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-25T21:31:47-07:00","id":1457681,"title":"Creating Prosthetics","content":"Hi. <br /> <br /> What spheres do you need to create technocratic prosthetics? You know, like the implants you buy with the Enhancement background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T06:13:10-07:00","id":1457704,"title":"","content":"It very much depends on what it does.<br /> <br /> Building the mechanicism of it might not even require Spheres if it's simple enough, and might really just be a Hypertech roll in a Technocracy lab.<br /> <br /> Installing it would require Life and Matter, and would cover some basic boosts.<br /> <br /> And additional Spheres as necessary to get it to do more than just replace a biological part with improved core functionality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T07:25:29-07:00","id":1457707,"title":"","content":"If they're being bought with the enhancements background, chances are good that they probably do need spheres. That said, they might be the cybernetic equivalent of trinkets, we're the only sphere you need is life. This is because the vast majority of such prosthetics imitate or enhance biological functions. The main exception to that would be various neural implants, which would tend to be based on mind instead. That said, these are just tendencies; and exceptions abound. <br /> <br /> Installation of a prosthetic is the technological equivalent of making a living thing into a Wonder, and requires life as per the living and virtual foundations box in book of secrets. You don't need matter any more than you would need matter to place a magical tattoo on someone, owing to ink being governed by matter. As mentioned before, whether or not you require prime depends entirely on whether or not the prosthetic counts as a trinket, as trinkets are one of two kinds of wonders that do not require Prime, and the other is not something that you're likely to see the technocracy dealing with (fetishes).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T14:35:08-07:00","id":1457734,"title":"","content":"So now for a third answer that differs from the first two\u2026<br /> <br /> To create cybernetics, you need Matter 3 and Prime 2 (if it can qualify as a Trinket) or Prime 4 (if not). You may need other spheres for complex cybernetics (perhaps Forces 2 and Mind 1 to create a DEI-like brain implant or Life 3 to create something that can increase physical attributes).<br /> <br /> To install cybernetics, you need Matter 3 and Life 3 (for yourself) or Life 4 (for someone else). Matter 3 is very specifically required as noted in the description of Matter\u2026 I\u2019m paraphrasing, but it says something like \u201ccombined with Life you can now fuse inanimate matter to living organisms \u201c.<br /> <br /> If you are buying them with the enhancements background, then you don\u2019t need to create or install them at all since it is part of your background. In this case someone else likely created and installed them for you. If you have the spheres to do so yourself then use your points at character creation for something else and just give yourself the upgrades in-game for free. You likewise do not need spheres to use cybernetic implants either, not if they\u2019re the real deal. A technocrat can also have \u201cfake\u201d implants that they use as an instrument for their spheres, and in this case I would argue that they can be created and implanted through mundane means without any spheres at all. By themselves they don\u2019t do anything and only you can activate them, but what you\u2019re actually doing is sphere magick\u2026 err\u2026 SCIENCE!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26904,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","user":"breggie","date":". 08-26-2021, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],